From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/display: parse AMD VSDB for HDMI FRL sinks

With DC_FRL_MASK set, FRL capable HDMI sinks are detected as
SIGNAL_TYPE_HDMI_FRL. amdgpu_dm_update_freesync_caps() only parsed the
AMD VSDB for SIGNAL_TYPE_HDMI_TYPE_A, so FreeSync over HDMI was never
reported (vrr_capable = 0) as soon as FRL was enabled. Use
dc_is_hdmi_signal() to cover both TMDS and FRL.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
@@ -14056,7 +14056,7 @@
 			amdgpu_dm_connector->as_type = ADAPTIVE_SYNC_TYPE_EDP;
 		}
 
-	} else if (drm_edid && sink->sink_signal == SIGNAL_TYPE_HDMI_TYPE_A) {
+	} else if (drm_edid && dc_is_hdmi_signal(sink->sink_signal)) {
 		i = parse_hdmi_amd_vsdb(amdgpu_dm_connector, edid, &vsdb_info);
 		if (i >= 0) {
 			amdgpu_dm_connector->vsdb_info = vsdb_info;
